<p>Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney said in a video address released Sunday that Canada’s close economic relationship with the United States, long seen as a national strength, has become “a weakness that must be corrected”. He said Ottawa needs to make the country less dependent on a single market because the US has changed its approach to trade, and Canada can no longer count on a return to the old status quo. Carney tied that shift to trade measures under President Trump, saying tariffs have hurt Canadian workers in manufacturing. His remarks came shortly after criticism from the US commerce secretary over Canada’s trade strategy, underscoring how tension with its largest trading partner is pushing Ottawa to rethink its economic model.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/J0OGV7nLsH2OOpLYYiQCYjZYi4A5ZNc_R9eOaR42109kXkRfChFpxn7DPrjFPWYgYHLE0GF3f6Sf_D5lBAuy8JS1KEdZ-W0AJIR2wBVuE4NKITEt5ZhjxMMlB3rAKSzx5peK8MdG80IL_ao2gjR16cEyRYGzojXPvF3vKkVKs2RtuX62BPqvFBaaPRjwFat0W2T5NbWYjk9_F-KhH4wLxsAm8CGitXBbrjpF3EUMMHqaqPGVPerE3i_7bw' alt='Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney during coverage related to Canada-US economic ties.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Recorded address: In a video of about 10 minutes released Sunday, Carney laid out the shift in approach.</li><li>Geopolitical framing: He cast diversification as part of adjusting to a less stable international environment, not just a response to tariffs.</li><li>Past threats: Carney said the moment feels unusual, but Canada has faced similar threats before, signaling confidence that the country can adapt again.</li><li>Practical agenda: He said his government is working to strengthen the economy by attracting new investment and signing trade deals with other countries.</li></ul><blockquote>The world is more dangerous and divided. - Mark Carney</blockquote><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/19/2026/mark-carney-calls-canadas-us-ties-a-weakness'>Mark Carney calls Canada&#x27;s US ties 